1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,495
Tumne AI assistant se bola, mera GitHub check karo, Slack pe update bhejo, aur calendar mein meeting daalo.

2
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:09,974
Usne jawab diya — sorry, main ye nahi kar sakta.

3
00:00:10,486 --> 00:00:10,765
Kyun?

4
00:00:11,363 --> 00:00:15,220
Kyunki LLM ek bahut smart dimaag hai, par uske haath nahi hain.

5
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:20,637
Har tool se baat karne ke liye developers ko alag alag custom integration likhna padta tha.

6
00:00:21,111 --> 00:00:25,614
Das AI apps aur das tools, matlab sau alag connectors.

7
00:00:26,259 --> 00:00:29,654
Yahin aata hai MCP — Model Context Protocol.

8
00:00:30,226 --> 00:00:33,452
Simple bhasha mein: AI ke liye USB-C port.

9
00:00:33,935 --> 00:00:36,769
Ek standard plug, jo har tool mein fit ho jaata hai.

10
00:00:37,437 --> 00:00:43,217
Pehle, har tool apna ek MCP Server banata hai, jo batata hai ki wo kya kya kar sakta hai.

11
00:00:43,765 --> 00:00:48,764
Tumhari AI app ke andar ek MCP Client hota hai, jo in servers se connect hota hai.

12
00:00:49,308 --> 00:00:57,270
Jab tum sawal poochte ho, LLM sahi tool chunta hai, client request bhejta hai, aur server real data ya action wapas laata hai.

13
00:00:57,858 --> 00:01:01,617
Na har app ke liye naya code, na har tool ke liye alag jugaad.

14
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:05,081
Ek baar server banao, har AI app use kar legi.

15
00:01:05,598 --> 00:01:08,239
Bas plug karo, aur AI ko haath mil jaate hain.
